.TITLE "nano"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
nano is a simple terminal text editor used on Linux and other Unix-like systems.

It is a good choice when you want to open and edit a file quickly without learning a lot first.
You can think of it as a basic editor that is easy to start using right away.

.DIV "EXAMPLE"
nano notes.txt

.DIV "EXPLANATION"
**nano** opens the file so you can edit it in the terminal.

Here, __nano__ is the editor.
__notes.txt__ is the file you are opening.

If the file does not exist yet, nano can create it when you save it.

.DIV "EXAMPLE"
nano myfile.txt

.DIV "EXPLANATION"
**nano** opens __myfile.txt__ so you can read or edit it.

This is useful when you want to quickly change a small file.

Remember to save your changes before leaving the editor.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
nano is a simple terminal editor for quick file edits.

Use it when you want something easy to open, edit, and save.
